$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM c. A mixture of 1.1 g (10 mmol) of 3-acetyl-1H-pyrazole (III) and 0.5 g
(10 mmol) of hydrazine hydrate in 3 ml of alcohol was heated for 30 min
at 70-80°C. The solvent was distilled off under reduced pressure, and the
residue was recrystallized from benzene. The product showed no depression
of the melting point on mixing with samples prepared as described above
in a and b. Its IR and 1H NMR spectra coincided with those of the
hydrazinolysis products of nitropyridines Ia and Ib.
1-(1H-Pyrazol-3-yl)ethanone hydrazone (II). Yield 1.2 g (97%). mp
147-149°C (from benzene). IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3320, 3175, 3125, 3030,
2970-2900, 2360, 2330, 1645, 1600, 1535, 1360, 1045, 800, 770, 700. 1H
NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 2.16 s (3H, CH3), 6.47 d (1H, 4-H, J = 2.2 Hz),
7.64 d (1H, 5-H, J = 2.2 Hz). Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel, %): 125 (100) [M
+ H]+, 123 (23) [M - H]+ , 108 (82) [M + H - NH3]+. Found, %: C 48.22; H
6.35; N 45.33. C5H8N4. Calculated, %: C 48.37; H 6.49; N 45.13. M 124.15.
mp 148-149°C
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
