$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 10 mL anhydrous ethanol, 0.05 g furfuraldehyde
and 0.18 g compound 2 were dissolved in a 25 mL round-bottom flask. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 min, after that
large amounts of precipitate formed. The reaction was performed for
further 0.5 h. The insoluble substance was filtrated with suction, washed
with anhydrous ethanol and recrystallized from DMF-ethanol-H2O to give 3a
as an acicular crystal (0.20 g). 3f, 96 %, white solid m.p. 161-163 °C;
1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300 MHz) δ: 11.11 (s, 1H, NH), 8.64 (s, 1H, CH=N),
6.94-7.86 (m, 7H, ArH), 3.57-4.10 (m, 16H, 4 × OCH2CH2O), 3.36 (s, 3H,
CH3O); 13C NMR δ: 161.7, 160.8, 152.1, 148.0, 130.5, 130.0, 128.3, 126.6,
126.3, 121.2, 114.4, 70.5, 69.6, 68.4, 55.3; IR (KBr) ν: 3186 (NH), 1604
(N=C), 1251, 1043 (Ar-O-CH2), 1138 (CH2-O-CH2) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 480.2
(M+, 2.06), 300.0 (7.54), 268.1 (18.48), 183.0 (11.31), 167.9 (21.89),
148.0 (34.07), 136.0 (61.45), 135.0 (29.84), 121.0 (100), 120.0 (79.56),
91.0 (40.34), 76.9 (39.22). Anal. calcd for C22H28N2SO8: C 54.99, H 5.87,
N 5.83; found C 54.72, H 5.88, N 6.02.
