$DATUM Reaction of 2 with Isatin and Isatoic Anhydride: Formation of 11 and 12 A
mixture of 2 (2.74 g, 0.01 mol) and isatin or isatoic anhydride (0.01
mol) was refluxed in dioxane (25 ml) for 3-5 hours (TLC). The solvent was
removed under vaccuo and the residue was recrystallized from DMF/water.
11 and 12, respectively.
3-({4-Amino-6-[2-(4-methoxyphenyl)vinyl)-5-oxo-4,5-dihydro[1,2,4]
triazin-3-yl} hydrazono)-1,3-dihydro-indol-2-one (11). (96%). m.p. >
300°C; MS: m/z 403 (M+, 100); IR (KBr), 1613 and 1716 (2CO), 3212 (NH2),
3303 (NH) cm-1; 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6) δ 3.42 (s, 3H, CH3O-4), 5.67 (s, 2H,
NH2), 6.81 (t, 2H, J = 4.4 Hz, Harom), 7.18 (t, 2H, J = 7.7 Hz, Harom),
7.54 (d, 2H, J = 3.6 Hz, Harom), 7.61 (q, 2H, J = 4.3 Hz, Harom), 7.76
(d, 2H, J = 8.3 Hz, Harom), 8.45 (d, 2H, 2NH), 10.59 (s, 1H, OH). Anal.
For C20H17N7O3 Calcd.: C, 59.55; H, 4.25; N, 24.31. Found: C, 59.47; H,
4.17; N, 24.22.
