$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Sugar Uracil-1-ylmethyl Hydrazones 4-5;
General Procedure To a well stirred solution of the respective
monosaccharide (2.80 mmol) and glacial AcOH (0.6 mL) in H2O (15 mL), was
added the appropriate 1-acetylhydrazinouracils 3a,b (2.80 mmol) in EtOH
(80 mL). The mixture was heated under reflux for 5 h (monitored by TLC)
and the resulting solution was concentrated under reduced pressure and
left to cool. The formed precipitate was filtered off, washed with H2O (5
mL) and EtOH (5 mL), dried and recrystallized from EtOH to give 4 and 5
in 88-95% yields. 5a, yield 92%. Mp (°C)a: 160-161; [α]D20(c 1, DMSO):
-12.5; Mol formula (mol wt): C12H18N4O7(330.29); Analysis (%,
Calcd/Found): C 43.64/43.51, H 5.49/5.37, N 16.96/16.77. m/z [M+]: 330.
1H NMR (DMSO-d6): 2.08 (s, 3 H, CH3), 3.38-3.55 (m, 4 H, H-3', H-4',
H-5'), 3.67 (m, 1 H, H-2'), 4.40 (br s, 1 H, OH), 4.61 (br s, 1 H, OH),
4.63 (s, 2 H, CH2), 4.75 (br s, 1 H, OH), 5.16 (br s, 1 H, OH), 7.50 (d,
J = 2.5 Hz, 1 H, H- 1'), 8.21 (s, 1 H, H-6), 11.19 (br s, 1 H, NH), 12.18
(br s, 1 H, NH) 13C NMR (DMSO-d6): 12.6 (CH3), 52.7 (CH2), 62.4 (C-5'),
67.2 (C-4'), 70.5 (C-2'), 71.9 (C-3'), 111.2 (C-5), 138.0 (C-6), 146.2
(C-1'), 150.0 (C-2), 164.0 (C-4), 166.7 (C=O).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and antiviral evaluation of sugar uracil-1-ylmethylhydrazones
and their oxadiazoline derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ali, Omar M.; Amer, Hamada H.; Abdel-Rahman, Adel A.-H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2007), (18), 2823-2828

