$DATUM 10 mL anhydrous ethanol, 0.05 g furfuraldehyde and 0.18 g compound 2 were
dissolved in a 25 mL round-bottom flask. The reaction mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 3 min, after that large amounts of precipitate
formed. The reaction was performed for further 0.5 h. The insoluble
substance was filtrated with suction, washed with anhydrous ethanol and
recrystallized from DMF-ethanol-H2O to give 3a as an acicular crystal
(0.20 g). 3a, 91 %, white solid m.p. 185-186 °C; 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300
MHz) δ: 11.28 (s, 1H, NH), 7.78 (s, 1H, CH=N), 6.56-7.42 (m, 6H, ArH),
3.35-4.12 (m, 16H, 4 × OCH2CH2O); 13C NMR δ: 152.2, 148.6, 148.0, 145.1,
136.9, 130.3, 121.1, 113.9, 112.4, 112.0, 111.6, 70.6, 69.6, 68.4; IR
(KBr) ν: 3163 (NH), 1585 (N=C), 1275, 1048 (Ar-O-CH2), 1142 (CH2-O-CH2)
cm-1; MS m/z (%): 440.2 (M+, 1.14), 412.1 (4.15), 376.1 (2.66), 369.4
(3.05), 368.3 (6.66), 331.1 (2.26), 300.1 (9.04), 268.1 (32.51), 224.0
(10.27), 183.0 (20.23), 167.9 (30.84), 136.0 (100), 120.9 (46.88), 80.9
(87.39), 79.9 (53.01), 51.9 (46.67). Anal. calcd for C19H24N2SO8: C
51.81, H 5.49, N 6.36; found C 51.79, H 5.26, N 6.13.
