$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 10 mL anhydrous ethanol, 0.05 g furfuraldehyde
and 0.18 g compound 2 were dissolved in a 25 mL round-bottom flask. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 min, after that
large amounts of precipitate formed. The reaction was performed for
further 0.5 h. The insoluble substance was filtrated with suction, washed
with anhydrous ethanol and recrystallized from DMF-ethanol-H2O to give 3a
as an acicular crystal (0.20 g). 3g, 89 %, yellow solid m.p. 187-190 °C;
1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300 MHz) δ: 10.85 (s, 1H, NH), 8.51 (s, 1H, CH=N),
6.67-7.77 (m, 7H, ArH), 3.57-4.11 (m, 16H, 4 × OCH2CH2O), 2.93 (s, 6H,
CH3); 13C NMR δ: 159.8, 152.0, 151.5, 148.2, 147.9, 130.6, 129.5, 128.1,
121.1, 112.4, 111.8, 70.5, 69.6, 68.4, 40.1; IR (KBr) ν: 3179 (NH), 1604
(N=C), 1273, 1043 (Ar-O-CH2), 1137 (CH2-O-CH2) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 493.1
(M+, 1.13), 465.3 (1.00), 368.4 (3.91), 329.1 (2.01), 300.1 (14.45),
294.1 (26.81), 268.2 25.37), 168.0 (49.35), 161.1 (15.87), 149.0 (32.86),
147.0 (28.75), 136.0 (100), 134.0 (41.47), 120.9 (61.94), 96.9 (36.14),
90.9 (42.37), 69.0 (41.70). Anal. calcd for C23H31N3SO7: C 55.97, H 6.33,
N 8.51; found C 56.08, H 6.09, N 8.57.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
