$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Condensation of 2 with Free Sugars: Formation
of 17a-f and 18 General Procedure A mixture of 2 (2.74 g, 0.01 mol) and
aldohexoses, namely: D-glucose, D-galactose, D-mannose, aldopentoses,
namely: D-ribose, L-arabinose, D-xylose, and/or fructose (0.01 mol) was
refluxed in dioxane (20 ml) for 4 horns (TLC). After cooling, the
precipitated solid was filtered off, washed with ethanol and
recrystallized from DMF. 17a-f and 18.
4-Amino-6-[2-(4-methoxyphenyl)vinyl]-3-[N'-(2,3,4,5,6-pentahydroxy-hexylidene)hydrazine]-4H-[1,2,4]triazin-5-one
(17b). Using D-galactose in the general procedure gave 17b. (88%). m.p.
177-179°C; MS: m/z 436 (M+, 16.30); IR (KBr), 1590 (CN), 3248 (NH2), 3368
(OH) cm-1; 1H NMR(DMSO-d 6): δ 2.95 (s, 3H, CH3O-4), 4.11-4.58 (m, 5H,
OH), 4.77 (m, 2H, H-5'), 5.38 (d, 1H, J = 2.76 Hz, H-4'), 5.61 (d, 1H, J
= 2.99 Hz, H-3'), 5.91 (d, 1H, J =2.33 Hz, H-2'), 6.11 (d, 1H, J =2.93
Hz, H-1'), 6.35 (s, 2H, NH2), 6.62 (s, H, NH), 7.38-7.63 (m, 6H, Harom),
8.38 (s, 1H, N = CH). Anal. For C18H24N6O7 Calcd.: C, 49.54; H, 5.54; N,
19.26. Found: C, 49.38; H, 5.49; N, 19.16.
