$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 10 mL anhydrous ethanol, 0.05 g furfuraldehyde
and 0.18 g compound 2 were dissolved in a 25 mL round-bottom flask. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 min, after that
large amounts of precipitate formed. The reaction was performed for
further 0.5 h. The insoluble substance was filtrated with suction, washed
with anhydrous ethanol and recrystallized from DMF-ethanol-H2O to give 3a
as an acicular crystal (0.20 g). 3c, 87.6 %, white solid m.p. 188-190 °C;
1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300 MHz) δ: 11.32 (s, 1H, NH), 7.91 (s, 1H, CH=N),
7.11-7.58 (m, 8H, ArH), 3.36-4.09 (m, 16H, 4 × OCH2CH2O); 13C NMR δ:
152.2, 148.0, 146.9, 133.7, 130.4, 130.1, 128.8, 126.7, 121.2, 112.4,
111.6, 70.5, 69.6, 68.4; IR (KBr) ν: 3181 (NH), 1585 (N=C), 1274, 1047
(Ar-O-CH2), 1139 (CH2-O-CH2) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 450.4 (0.76), 422.0
(2.20), 385.3 (1.22), 368.4 (5.84), 332.2 (1.36), 313.3 (1.61), 300.1
(9.56), 268.1 (25.87), 213.2 (10.94), 185.1 (15.08), 168.0 (30.51), 136.0
(81.14), 121.0 (48.31), 118.0 (64.80), 111.9 (25.05), 97.0 (33.70), 90.0
(100), 88.9 (98.07), 69.0 (36.69), 54.9 (39.69). Anal. calcd for
C21H26N2SO7: C 55.99, H 5.82, N 6.22; found C 56.12, H 5.75, N 6.21.
