$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 10 mL anhydrous ethanol, 0.05 g furfuraldehyde
and 0.18 g compound 2 were dissolved in a 25 mL round-bottom flask. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 min, after that
large amounts of precipitate formed. The reaction was performed for
further 0.5 h. The insoluble substance was filtrated with suction, washed
with anhydrous ethanol and recrystallized from DMF-ethanol-H2O to give 3a
as an acicular crystal (0.20 g). 3d, 83 %, white solid m.p. 165-166 °C;
1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300 MHz) δ: 11.34 (s, 1H, NH), 10.26 (s, 1H, OH), 8.17
(s, 1H, CH=N), 6.81-7.49 (m, 7H, ArH), 3.37-4.12 (m, 16H, 4 x OCH2CH2O);
13C NMR δ: 156.5, 152.3, 148.1, 146.3, 131.5, 130.0, 127.6, 121.2, 119.4,
119.0, 116.2, 112.5, 111.5, 70.5, 69.6, 68.4; IR (KBr) ν: 3173 (NH), 1581
(N=C), 1269, 1042 (Ar-O-CH2), 1139 (CH2-O-CH2) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 466.2
(M+, 5.13), 347.0 (4.76), 315.0 (8.54), 300.0 (11.10), 268.1 (28.14),
214.9 (25.13), 182.9 (31.51), 167.9 (38.34), 135.9 (100), 120.9 (50.72),
105.9 (76.22), 77.9 (55.68). Anal. calcd for C21H26N2SO8: C 54.07, H
5.62, N 6.01; found C 54.19, H 5.66, N 6.12.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
