$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Condensation of 2 with Free Sugars: Formation of 17a-f and 18 General
Procedure A mixture of 2 (2.74 g, 0.01 mol) and aldohexoses, namely:
D-glucose, D-galactose, D-mannose, aldopentoses, namely: D-ribose,
L-arabinose, D-xylose, and/or fructose (0.01 mol) was refluxed in dioxane
(20 ml) for 4 horns (TLC). After cooling, the precipitated solid was
filtered off, washed with ethanol and recrystallized from DMF. 17a-f and
18.
4-Amino-6-[2-(4-methoxypheny])vinyl]-3-[N'-(2,3,4,5,6-pentahydroxy-hexylidene)hydrazine]-4H-[1,2,4]triazin-5-one
(17a). Using D-glucose in the general procedure gave 17a. (82%). m.p.
195-196°C; IR (KBr), 1600 (CN), 3208 (NH2), 3425 (OH) cm-1; 1H NMR
(DMSO-d 6) δ 2.51 (s, 3H, CH3O-4), 3.67-3.75 (m, 4H, OH), 3.89 (s, 1H,
OH), 4.35 (d, 2H, J = 5.36 Hz, H-5'), 4.49 (dd, 1H, J = 2.97 Hz, H-4'),
4.85 (dd, 1H, J H-3'-H-4' = 2.18 Hz, J H-3'-H-2' = 9.36 Hz, H-3'), 5.03
(t, 1H, J =2.07, H-2'), 5.25 (s, 2H, NH2), 5.68 (d, 1H, J =2.78, H-1'),
5.72 (s, H, NH), 6.91-7.13 (m, 6H, Harom), 7.69 (s, 1H, N = CH). Anal.
For C18H24N6O7 Calcd.: C, 49.54; H, 5.54; N, 19.26. Found: C, 49.98; H,
5.72; N, 18.67.
