$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 10 mL anhydrous ethanol, 0.05 g furfuraldehyde
and 0.18 g compound 2 were dissolved in a 25 mL round-bottom flask. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 min, after that
large amounts of precipitate formed. The reaction was performed for
further 0.5 h. The insoluble substance was filtrated with suction, washed
with anhydrous ethanol and recrystallized from DMF-ethanol-H2O to give 3a
as an acicular crystal (0.20 g). 3h, 81 %, white solid m.p. 208-209 °C;
1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300 MHz) δ: 11.01 (s, 1H, NH), 9.52 (s, 1H, OH), 7.79
(s, 1H, CH = N), 6.76-7.45 (m, 6H, ArH), 3.58-4.10 (m, 16H, 4 ×
OCH2CH2O), 3.42 (s, 3H, CH3O); 13C NMR δ: 152.1, 148.9, 148.0, 147.9,
147.7, 130.5, 125.1, 121.3, 121.2, 115.4, 112.4, 111.8, 109.3, 70.5,
69.6, 68.4, 55.5; IR (KBr) ν: 3186 (NH), 1593 (N=C), 1281, 1040
(Ar-O-CH2), 1137 (CH2-O-CH2) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 496.2 (M+, 0.44), 468.1
(2.86), 300.0 (9.46), 269.1 (3.38), 268.1 (18.32), 182.9 (14.08), 168.0
(26.15), 163.9 (12.64), 151.0 (11.78), 137.0 (100), 136.0 (94.46), 120.9
(27.43), 106.9 (29.36), 79.9 (15.38). Anal. calcd for C22H28N2SO9: C
53.22, H 5.68, N 5.64; found C 53.39, H 5.62, N 5.68.
